    "title": "Someone parked across my driveway and blocked me in. I was late for work. - NewsBreak",
    "text": "13 hours ago Photo by Google I walked out at 7:30 AM, coffee in hand, ready to leave. A shiny red sports car was parked directly across the bottom of my driveway. Not just a little bit—completely blocking me in. I was furious. I honked. No answer. I walked to the nearest houses, knocking on doors. No one claimed it. I was about to call a tow truck, which takes hours and creates a huge scene. Instead, I snapped a picture of the car and license plate and posted it on LocalAll : \"Does this car belong to your guest? They are blocking me in, and the tow truck is on speed dial.\" Five minutes later, a young man came sprinting out of a house three doors down. He looked terrified. \"I'm so sorry!\" he yelled. \"I didn't realize how far back I pulled up. I'm moving it now!\" He saw the notification on his host's phone. Problem solved in 5 minutes, no police needed. Solve disputes fast without the drama. Use LocalAll.\n87",
